    "body": "### Problem\n\n`vim.pack.add()` [rewrites](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/fbcb7a056cef7a5efd7aa7f494365a04b1c86895/runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua#L1070) `nvim-pack-lock.json` after installing plugins into an empty data directory, \neven when the lockfile already contains the exact source, revision, and pinned version that were installed.\n\nThis prevents using `vim.pack` with a read-only configuration directory. \nPlugin installation itself succeeds in the writable data directory, \nbut startup then fails when Neovim attempts to rewrite the unchanged lockfile.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate `init.lua`\n\n```lua\n vim.pack.add({\n    {\n      src = 'https://github.com/nvim-lua/plenary.nvim',\n      version = '50012918b2fc8357b87cff2a7f7f0446e47da174',\n    },\n  }, {\n    confirm = false,\n  })\n```\n\nCreate `nvim-pack-lock.json` and make it read-only for the neovim process.\n```\n  {\n    \"plugins\": {\n      \"plenary.nvim\": {\n        \"rev\": \"50012918b2fc8357b87cff2a7f7f0446e47da174\",\n        \"src\": \"https://github.com/nvim-lua/plenary.nvim\",\n        \"version\": \"'50012918b2fc8357b87cff2a7f7f0446e47da174'\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n```\n\nStart neovim and get\n\n```\n  Error in .../config/nvim/init.lua:\n  E5113: Lua chunk: .../runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:834:\n  EACCES: permission denied: .../config/nvim/nvim-pack-lock.json\n  stack traceback:\n          [C]: in function 'assert'\n          .../runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:834: in function 'lock_write'\n          .../runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:933: in function 'lock_sync'\n          .../runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:969: in function 'lock_read'\n          .../runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:1010: in function 'add'\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nProcess does not error.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nmaster\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nnot relevant\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nnot relevant\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nnot relevant\n\n### Installation\n\nnot relevant ",
